<title>EGYPT: Egypt cotton export prices steady.</title>
<headline>Egypt cotton export prices steady.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Export prices rose for three grades of Egyptian cotton this week and the rest were unchanged from two weeks ago, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Monday.</p>
<p>An Alcotexa official said they have stopped exporting Giza 86 because stocks had run out.</p>
<p>The prices in centilibres (valid until 2200 GMT December 7) are -</p>
<p>	     FG/EX    FG+1/4     FG     FG-1/4    G/FG    G+3/8</p>
<p> Giza 76   173.0    167.0    161.0    155.0    149.0    146.0</p>
<p> Giza 70   166.0    160.0    154.0    148.0    142.0    139.0</p>
<p> Giza 77   162.0    156.0    150.0    144.0    138.0    135.0</p>
<p> Giza 75   134.0    128.0    122.0    116.0    110.0    107.0</p>
<p> Giza 85   131.0    125.0    119.0    113.0    107.0    104.0</p>
<p> Giza 83   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p> Giza 80   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p>Note - FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
